From ba886522c6fe7679440e92618d983876f243bbe4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 05:17:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: the provenance record of the two headers says
 they are written again

PROVENANCE.json described dvbridge_metadata.h and mpv_dvbridge_cm4.h as derived from intel-dv-linux
under GPL-3.0-or-later, with the CM v4.0 helper kept verbatim. Since the previous commit neither holds
code of that source: the record now says so and gives their licence, GPL-2.0-or-later, and keeps the
earlier description as their history. Nothing reads this file; it is a record.
---
 tools/dvbridge/PROVENANCE.json | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/PROVENANCE.json b/tools/dvbridge/PROVENANCE.json
index 80aaf17..8138bb0 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/PROVENANCE.json
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/PROVENANCE.json
@@ -1,12 +1,14 @@
 {
   "source": "intel-dv-linux source-manifest.json",
   "changes": "Player-specific GPU state and rendering entry points removed; metadata functions made header-local; geometry and bounds validation adapted for the shared transactional API. CM4 helper retained verbatim. Release preparation removes the optional per-frame payload trace; transport calculations are unchanged.",
-  "license": "GPL-3.0-or-later",
+  "license": "GPL-2.0-or-later",
+  "license_before": "GPL-3.0-or-later",
   "integrated_into_kodi": true,
   "scope": "Derivation record for these two headers, not a complete third-party provenance clearance or hardware qualification.",
   "upstream_files_sha256": {
     "dvbridge_metadata.h": "bc38347df1488546b80fe0e7613840a0437a7f075c9bac114e1f9111c9e99196",
     "mpv_dvbridge_cm4.h": "f6762808f5d7a5824983d72b0188098f19e86bd2a6db7b997ef63e2d35612661"
   },
-  "note": "upstream_files_sha256 are the SHA-256 of the two headers as they were integrated (the derivation described above), not of the files in this tree: LibreELEC Hades changed both since (the git history of this directory says what and why), so these hashes are not expected to match them. The changes after integration (scene refresh in microseconds and by the frame period, L255 and reserved levels left out, the L1 average clamped, level 5 offsets of a cropped or scaled master, a payload of up to 512 bytes in packets of four bytes to a word, the metadata id that goes on across streams, the level 11 checks of dovi_tool, metadata without extension blocks readable, the content mapping v4.0 part left out for a display of display management 2 or 3, the trims left out for a display that is to be sent none) are Hades' own and do not come from that source."
+  "note": "upstream_files_sha256 are the SHA-256 of the two headers as they were integrated (the derivation described above), not of the files in this tree: LibreELEC Hades changed both since (the git history of this directory says what and why), so these hashes are not expected to match them. The changes after integration (scene refresh in microseconds and by the frame period, L255 and reserved levels left out, the L1 average clamped, level 5 offsets of a cropped or scaled master, a payload of up to 512 bytes in packets of four bytes to a word, the metadata id that goes on across streams, the level 11 checks of dovi_tool, metadata without extension blocks readable, the content mapping v4.0 part left out for a display of display management 2 or 3, the trims left out for a display that is to be sent none) are Hades' own and do not come from that source.",
+  "rewritten": "Since 2026-11-04 neither header holds code of that source: the parts of dvbridge_metadata.h that came from it, and the whole of mpv_dvbridge_cm4.h, were written again from ETSI GS CCM 001 V1.1.1 clause 6 and the field layouts of dovi_tool (MIT), by writers that had not seen the earlier code, with the same bytes out (the commit that did it says how that was measured). Both are under GPL-2.0-or-later. The record above is the history of how the two headers came here."
 }
-- 
